    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Writing Skills Resource Path"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "All new engineering students are automatically enrolled in CEN 199 : Writing Skills.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "CEN 199",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/common-engineering/CEN/199/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "CEN 199 is graded on a Pass/Fail basis, and is used to track the results of the Writing Skills Test (WST).",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "CEN 199",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/common-engineering/CEN/199/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "All students admitted into engineering are required to write the mandatory Writing Skills Test (WST) during Orientation Week. Students who pass the WST (by achieving a grade of ‘B' or higher) will receive a PASS in CEN 199 and therefore may enrol in the lower level liberal studies course of their choice (subject to availability).",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "CEN 199",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/common-engineering/CEN/199/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students who do not pass the WST will receive an INP (In Progress Grade) in CEN 199 and will be required to enrol in one of LNG 111 , LNG 112 , LNG 113 , or LNG 121 as their first-year lower level liberal studies course. These courses, which count toward lower level liberal studies requirements, are writing-intensive humanities and social science courses designed to give students the opportunity to strengthen their foundations in communication. These students will then have three additional opportunities to write and pass the WST:",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "CEN 199",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/common-engineering/CEN/199/"
        },
        {
          "text": "LNG 111",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/language/LNG/111/"
        },
        {
          "text": "LNG 112",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/language/LNG/112/"
        },
        {
          "text": "LNG 113",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/language/LNG/113/"
        },
        {
          "text": "LNG 121",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/language/LNG/121/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "In May, following 2nd Semester."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "During Orientation Week before 3rd Semester."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "In May, following 4th Semester."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "A PASS in CEN 199 : Writing Skills is required to enrol in all third-year engineering courses. Students with a grade of INP in CEN 199 will not be allowed to enrol in any third-year engineering course.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "CEN 199",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/common-engineering/CEN/199/"
        },
        {
          "text": "CEN 199",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/common-engineering/CEN/199/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Detailed information is available from the First-Year Engineering Office. Room ENG 377 Telephone: 416-979-5000 ext. 554261."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Optional Specialization in Engineering Innovation and Entrepreneurship (OS EIE)"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "This option provides students with a solid foundation in innovation and entrepreneurship theory as well as the immersive experience of advancing and shaping an idea into a business. The lecture courses cover principles of engineering economics, entrepreneurship and innovation management, and technology based new venture creation. The practicum will guide students through the process of identifying a new business concept, developing their technology, and preparing their business for market readiness. For eligibility, registration and course information see Optional Specialization in Engineering Innovation and Entrepreneurship (OS EIE) .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Optional Specialization in Engineering Innovation and Entrepreneurship (OS EIE)",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/optional-specializations/engineering_innovation/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Optional Specialization in Management Sciences (OS MS)"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students can enrich their studies and hone their management skills with the Optional Specialization in Management Sciences. Courses within the optional specialization cover four major areas in management sciences: Strategic Engineering Management, Operations Management/Operations Research, Finance, and Organizational Behaviour. For eligibility, registration, and course information see Optional Specialization in Management Sciences (OS MS) .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Optional Specialization in Management Sciences (OS MS)",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/optional-specializations/management_sciences/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Engineering Transfer Credits"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Applicants approved into an Engineering program cannot expect to receive any transfer credits in Engineering discipline or Engineering related discipline courses if their applicable post-secondary education was not completed at a program accredited by the Canadian Engineering Accreditation Board (external link, opens in new window) (CEAB).",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Canadian Engineering Accreditation Board (external link, opens in new window)",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/accreditation/accredited-programs"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Core and professional engineering course transfer credits will ONLY be granted at the time of admission. An Offer of Admission will notify the applicant of transfer credit decision(s) subject to acceptance of their Offer."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Liberal studies discipline courses taken at CEAB accredited or non-accredited schools will be considered for either lower- or upper-level liberal studies transfer credit. College courses, in general, are not eligible for transfer credit except in the case of lower-level liberal studies courses."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Liberal Studies"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students must take two lower level liberal studies courses and two upper level liberal studies courses to graduate. Students must not choose courses that are restricted for their program or major.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "lower level",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/liberal-studies/table_a/"
        },
        {
          "text": "upper level",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/liberal-studies/table_b/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Please refer to the liberal studies chapter of this calendar for more information on the Liberal Studies Policy. Further information on liberal studies can also be found at the Faculty of Arts' Liberal Studies website (opens in new window) .",
